ype of a  conversation and you know the  speculation of trump with adult adhd or  whatever i think the guy just has no  idea what's going on in any serious  depth with any topic i think that's  really the explanation and trump would  ramble on and interrupt and interject  about the election stolen or whatever so  from like a conversational standpoint  i don't know how trump does  a three-hour conversation with rogan  that's not a praise or a criticism of  the format i think it's a great  it's great to have podcasts of all  different formats and the three hour  conversation is a great format for  people who can do it it doesn't seem to  me that that trump could do it now in  terms of rogan  doesn't want to help trump as i've said  before  i don't think there's any  like big mystery  about rogan  i think  rogan admits  he's not the most keyed into politics  and rogan to a degree is a chameleon of  sorts when i was on his show and i  espoused all of my left-wing ideas  joe agreed with almost everything i had  to say  and then when he has on you know whoever  from the right  he agrees generally with most of the  things they have to say he's had  disagreements that i've covered with  people like um  he's had disagreements with ben shapiro  on some things he's had disagreements  with candace owens you know  right-wingers in a sense  and to a degree i think that what's  happening with rogan is  he is um  when it comes to a lot of different  areas he is clearly on the left when you  get into the details i think he  genuinely is  i think he's also culturally  conservative a lot of the circles he's  now in  you know ufc and dana white  definite right wing uh bent there he's  now in texas and reportedly i think has  a relationship with the governor there  greg abbott who's an extreme right  winger  he's in this environment where there's a  lot of kind of de facto right wing  thinking and then like on desantis i  just think he's sort of confused i don't  even think rogan is aware that desantis  stands for the opposite of most of the  things rogan has espoused support for so  i don't think we need to get into this  thing of like ascribing  a significant morality to it i think  politics isn't rogan's main thing  and he finds common ground with almost  anyone he talks to  and while he is socially liberal to a  great degree  he's also in a culturally conservative  environment and that rubs off on him so  interesting for sure how much we glean  from it about anything in particular  other than trump's desperation to get on  rogan's podcast which is interesting uh  is probably not too too much  as many of you know i take my snacks  very seriously i avoid excess sugar and  junk food and so when i want something  sweet  i go to our sponsor monk pack monk pack  makes my favorite granola bars and nut  and seed bars if you're doing keto it  works just one gram of sugar or less  only two to three net carbs under 150  calories the flavors are delicious sea  salt dark chocolate that's my favorite  you've got your coconut cocoa chip  you've got your caramel sea salt the  texture the flavors this is a beautiful  granola bar and then you've got monk  packs nut and seed bars which are more  crunchy if you're craving something like  a crunchy chocolate candy bar  monk pack is the perfect thing to grab  instead same taste same experience none  of the carbs and sugars and calories  get 20 off your first order at  monkpack.com using the code pacman at  checkout the link is down below

